// Tauride Garden data: the POND DATUM TABLE (docs/TAURIDE-REMAKE.md, phase T4a). Hand-authored (NOT generated by tools/tauride/build.mjs), pure data: no imports. THE one place where the water of the garden gets its numbers:
// the height function (height.js: the bowls and the banks), the water surface (ponds.js), the shore colliders, the ground material (the wet band, the bed), the water mask and the tests are all DERIVED from this table. The old
// module's datums disagreed (water -0.55, ground cut -0.4, bed -1.4, shore box up to +0.22), which made the wading trap: do not add a second copy of a number that is here.
// Frame: metres from ORIGIN, y = 0 is the street level. DESIGN values (no survey of the ponds exists): the plan's "water -0.45, bed -1.2 / -0.5, bank top +0.1, bank slope 1:3 .. 1:5" (docs/TAURIDE-REMAKE.md section 7).
// The shape (height.js `pondProfile`) from the shore line out, d = the signed distance to the water outline (data/water.js WATER_UNION: + on land, - in the water), s = the local bank slope (the run per metre of height):
//   in the water   h = WATER_Y - u / s  (u = -d) down to the bed, the bed reached by a rounded knee (BED_KNEE: a quadratic fillet, so the mesh stays within 5 cm at a 1 m leaf)
//   on land        h = WATER_Y + (BANK_TOP - WATER_Y) * (1 - (1 - d / D)^2) up to d = D = 2 (BANK_TOP - WATER_Y) s (a quadratic ease: the slope at the waterline is exactly 1 : s, so the land side meets the straight slope of the water side without a kink; the crest is level), then the crest falls to the lawn
//                  (0) over CREST_FALL m on a smoothstep; the relief of data/relief.js is ADDED on land (it is zero within 3 m of the water by its own rules).
// s varies slowly along the shore between SLOPE_MIN and SLOPE_MAX (a smooth product of two sines of the position: no two stretches of bank look alike).

/** metres: the one water level of the garden (the water surface mesh, the waterline of the profile) */
export const WATER_Y = -0.45;
/** metres: the bed of the Big Pond (the lake r1582714 with the east and the south arm) */
export const BED_BIG = -1.2;
/** metres: the bed of the Small Pond (the west pond r6278222 and its canal to the dam): 5 cm of water over the mud, a duckweed pond */
export const BED_SMALL = -0.5;
/** metres: the crest of the bank */
export const BANK_TOP = 0.1;
/** the bank slope 1 : s along the shore varies between these (1:3 steep .. 1:5 gentle) */
export const SLOPE_MIN = 3;
export const SLOPE_MAX = 5;
/** metres: the crest falls from BANK_TOP to the lawn (0) over this distance (smoothstep) */
export const CREST_FALL = 3;
/** the knee of the bed: the fraction of the run (depth * s) over which the bank rounds into the flat bed (quadratic fillet, 0.5 = the knee spans the run) */
export const BED_KNEE = 1;
/** the slow variation of the slope along the shore: s = SLOPE_MIN + (SLOPE_MAX - SLOPE_MIN) * n(x, z), n = 0.5 + 0.5 sin(x kx + px) sin(z kz + pz) in [0, 1] (rad per metre, rad) */
export const SLOPE_NOISE = { kx: 0.047, px: 0.9, kz: 0.039, pz: -0.4 };

/** The Small Pond: the part of the water where the bed is BED_SMALL. A point is Big (weight 1) east of EAST_X and south of MOUTH_Z, both edges smoothstepped over BLEND m; everywhere else the bed is BED_SMALL.
 *  MOUTH_Z: the west pond meets the lake in a 10 m channel at z = -1655.3 (x 1268.8 .. 1278.6, the OSM outlines of r6278222 / r1582714 share it); EAST_X: no Small Pond water lies east of x 1250 south of the mouth. */
export const SMALL_POND = { mouthZ: -1655.3, eastX: 1250, blendZ: 4, blendX: 8 };

/** The shore colliders (ponds.js): boxes along the shore contour at COLLIDER.contourY (the ground height of the line they stand on; the box stands INLAND of the line, its water-side face on it), `thick` metres thick, from `y0` to `top`.
 *  physics.js: a box blocks a walker whose feet + STEP_HEIGHT (0.45) is below its top, at every feet height down to y0: top = 1.8 blocks everything up to feet 1.35 m (a jump from the crest, apex +0.73, cannot clear it) and the
 *  bed (-1.2) lies above y0. Segments are merged while the chord stays within `chord` m of the contour and shorter than `maxLen`; `gap` m is added at both ends (no wedge between neighbours). */
export const COLLIDER = { contourY: -0.3, top: 1.8, y0: -2.5, thick: 0.4, chord: 0.12, maxLen: 14, gap: 0.3 };

/** The ground material (ground-material.js): the wet band at the waterline and the colours of the bed, from the mask's signed shore distance (+ land) */
export const WET_BAND = 0.5;            // metres of darker, wet ground on the land side of the waterline
export const SHORE_SAND = 0.9;          // metres: the narrow pale sand / silt strip above the wet band (the shore line of a pond)
export const BED_COLORS = { mud: '#3b3a26', silt: '#5a5232', wet: '#4a4a30', sand: '#8a7f5a' };

/** The water surface (ponds.js) and its material (environment/water.js LOOK key `tauride-pond`) */
export const WATER_LOOK_KEY = 'tauride-pond';
/** the duckweed band of the Small Pond: a green mat on the water that is within `band` m of the bank, `cover` its share at the bank (0 .. 1) */
export const DUCKWEED = { band: 6, cover: 0.85 };

/** Where the water ends up for the other systems (the water mask / env.waterAt, the pedestrians): the shore distance below which a point counts as water */
export const MASK_SHORE = 0;
